        "comments": "The assembly ddEmpNigr1.hap1.1 is based on 41x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and chloroplast genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. There is a haplotypic inversion on Chromosome 9 HAP1 when compared to the other haplotypes from 6.45 to 11.70 Mbp. A second haplotypic inversion was detected on Chromosome 8 from 11.44 to 17.36 Mbp. The Chromosome 9 regions from 6.48 to 7.38 and from 10.03 to 10.73 Mbp seem to be present in HAP1 only.The following regions are highly repetitive and the order and orientation may be uncertain:Chromosome 1 from 28.14 to 29.47 MbpChromosome 3 from 23.85 to 27.32 MbpChromosome 7 from 11.67 to 12.25 MbpChromosome 8 from 22.26 to 27.63 Mbp",
